  "proof": "For N=weight(value)>=1 (one per node plus UTF8 key/string bytes), evaluator cost <=C(schema)*N. Refs/branches add, array items use maximum child coefficient times total item weight, object named properties use maximum and pattern/propertyName/additional use summed conservative coefficients. Constants/required/order annotations are fixed costs amortized by N. uniqueItems canonical output <=32*item weight for exact JSON integers/model, and its extra value scan costs item weight. Full input precharge adds N. For strict byte-free deterministic CBOR, N<=encoded payload length. Failed parses/operational errors do not imply schema success. This bounds meter credits, not wall-clock time or allocations; original NFC/transport/depth/context gates remain required."
